-- title:
--   Three-party inner region from the two receiving orders
-- statement:
--   Let $|\psi\rangle^{AC_A BC_B CR}$ be normalized and pure on nonzero finite registers. Alice initially holds $AC_A$, Bob holds $BC_B$, Charlie holds $C$, and $R$ is inaccessible. The goal is to send $C_A,C_B$ to Charlie. Let $r=(Q_{A\to C},Q_{B\to C},E_{AC},E_{BC})$, with signed initial-minus-final Bell costs and entropies in bits.
--
--   For a transfer with retained sender register $S$, message subsystem $T$, receiver side information $V$, and inaccessible remainder $W$, put $q=I(T;W\mid V)/2$ and $e=[I(T;S)-I(T;V)]/2$. Let $r^{AB}$ be the four costs obtained by applying this rule first to $(S,T,V,W)=(A,C_A,C,BC_BR)$, then to $(B,C_B,C_AC,AR)$. Let $r^{BA}$ be obtained first from $(B,C_B,C,AC_AR)$, then from $(A,C_A,C_BC,BR)$, placing each link's costs in the same order as $r$.
--
--   Every rate of the form
--   $$
--   r=t\,r^{AB}+(1-t)r^{BA}+d,\qquad 0\le t\le1,
--   $$
--   where
--   $$
--   d_{Q_A}\ge0,\quad d_{Q_B}\ge0,\quad d_{Q_A}+d_{E_{AC}}\ge0,\quad d_{Q_B}+d_{E_{BC}}\ge0,
--   $$
--   is achievable by finite local CPTP encoders, two separately charged forward quantum messages, and Charlie's decoder. Achievability means vanishing joint full trace-norm error on the full source and both returned Bell banks at every sufficiently large positive blocklength, with arbitrary positive rate slack.
--
--   Time sharing and resource substitution yield this inner region. No equality with the full three-party optimum is asserted; the paper explicitly allows further strategies to enlarge it.
-- source:
--   The operational meaning of quantum conditional information, arXiv:quant-ph/0612050v2, PDF p. 4, three-party-achievable-region

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Gap48_P20

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P20

open scoped Matrix ComplexConjugate

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P39 (rectAct)

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable Classical.decEq

section ThreePartyCorners

variable {A CA B CB C R : Type*}

variable [Fintype A] [Fintype CA] [Fintype B] [Fintype CB] [Fintype C] [Fintype R]

/-- Three-party achievable region, PDF p.4: every cost generated by the two
orders is achievable. The source explicitly allows other strategies to enlarge
this region, so no converse or equality with the full region is asserted. -/
theorem threePartyInnerRegion [Nonempty A] [Nonempty CA] [Nonempty B]
    [Nonempty CB] [Nonempty C] [Nonempty R]
    (psi : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ThreeSource A CA B CB C R)) (hpsi : IsState psi)
    (rates : Fin 4 → ℝ) (hrates : InGeneratedRegion psi rates) :
    ThreePartyAchievable psi rates := by sorry

end ThreePartyCorners

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P20

end
